=== JSON_SHAPE ===
PRE-MIGRATION List response (per src/code reading):
  []  // when no rows, returns empty array (rows == nil branch)
  [{ts, created_at, id, playback_status?, now_playing_title?, now_playing_artist?, now_playing_album?, playback_source?, audio_volume?, audio_volume_max?, audio_volume_increment?, now_playing_station?, now_playing_duration?, now_playing_elapsed?}, ...]
  - 'ts' is RFC3339Nano timestamp (date_trunc'd to second by SignalTracePivot)
  - 'created_at' = duplicate of 'ts' (added in handler loop)
  - 'id' = 1-indexed sequence number (added in handler loop)
  - field keys present only when the signal appeared at-or-near that timestamp (no carry-forward in old impl)

POST-MIGRATION List response (verified by handler code):
  []  // empty rows
  [{ts, created_at, id, <field>: <value>, ...}, ...]
  - 'ts' is row.Timestamp (RFC3339Nano)
  - 'created_at' = same as 'ts'
  - 'id' = 1-indexed sequence number
  - field keys present per StateReader.Timeline projection (forward-folded — fields carry-forward from prior rows)
  - same JSON envelope shape; bug-fix is in PAYLOAD CONTENT (rows are no longer mostly-empty; collapse drops phantom-duplicate rows)

PRE-MIGRATION Latest response:
  {} // when snap empty
  {playback_status?, now_playing_title?, ...11 keys}  // only present-in-snap keys

POST-MIGRATION Latest response:
  {playback_status: nil|val, now_playing_title: nil|val, ..., now_playing_elapsed: nil|val}  // ALL 11 canonical keys ALWAYS PRESENT
  - INTENTIONAL: empty-state policy upgrade. Frontend already handles per-field nil; absent keys would crash UI on edge cases.
  - Backwards-compatible: existing payloads with all 11 keys present are unchanged (same key set, same value semantics).
  - New behavior: empty/partial states now emit nil-filled canonical shape instead of {} or partial map.

